## Security Summary

| Rule | Implementation |
|------|----------------|
| **No XSS** | All user data HTML-escaped via `escapeHtml()` before interpolation; templates use allowlisted keys only |
| **No injection** | Template variables strictly allowlisted; custom templates validated against dangerous patterns |
| **Server-side only** | Email generation and sending happens server-side; client calls API endpoint |
| **Authorization** | Users can only send emails to themselves (verified via session); admins can send to others |
| **Rate limiting** | Per-recipient rate limiting (10 emails/hour) |
| **Secrets** | Email API keys only in server environment variables, never in client bundle |
| **CSP compatible** | Templates use inline styles only (no external CSS/JS); no unsafe patterns |
| **Structured logging** | Errors logged as structured objects, not interpolated strings |

## Usage

```typescript
// Server-side usage (API routes, server actions, etc.)
import { NotificationService } from '@/lib/email/notification-service';
import { getUserProfile } from '@/lib/db/user';

const emailSender = createEmailSender(); // Your provider
const notifications = new NotificationService(emailSender);

// Send welcome email
const user = await getUserProfile(userId);
await notifications.sendTemplatedEmail('welcome', user);

// Send password reset
await notifications.sendTemplatedEmail('passwordReset', user, {
  resetUrl: `https://app.com/reset?token=${generateSecureToken()}`,
});

// Send custom notification
await notifications.sendTemplatedEmail('notification', user, {
  notificationTitle: 'New feature available',
  notificationMessage: 'Check out our new dashboard!',
});
```

The implementation follows all security rules: no client-side secrets, server-side authorization with ownership checks in WHERE clause, bound parameters (via ORM), HTML escaping on all user data, allowlisted template keys, validated custom templates, rate limiting, and structured logging.
